# rtlmd — Development & Production Rules

Static PWA + Electron app. App sources are split; runtime loads bundles.

## JS: edit sources, never the bundle

- Edit ONLY `app/js/src/core/*.js` and `app/js/src/extras/*.js`.
- NEVER hand-edit `app/js/rtlmd.bundle.js`.
- Local dev: keep `npm run watch:js` running (`scripts/watch-js.mjs` rebuilds
  the bundle on every save) — then the loop is just save → refresh browser.
- Without the watcher (or before commit/release): `npm run build:js`.
- The builder (`scripts/build-js-bundle.mjs`) concatenates core→extras
  alphabetically, wraps in one IIFE, runs `node --check`, and FAILS on
  duplicate top-level functions.
- The bundle is committed: the app must run straight from git, no build needed.
- No ES `import/export` at runtime (Electron uses `loadFile` = `file://`;
  modules are CORS-blocked). Classic scripts only; lazy-load via injected
  `<script>` tags (same-origin, SW-precached), like `ensureWordBundle()`.
- No duplicated helpers: shared code lives ONCE (e.g. storage helpers in
  `core/10-markdown.js`). extras talk to core via `window.rtlmd*` hooks +
  the `rtlmdApi` object built in `core/90-boot.js` — keep that contract.

## CSS: 9 split sheets, order matters

- `app/css/00-tokens-base.css` … `08-settings.css`. Keep `<link>` order in
  `index.html` numeric — cascade depends on it.
- `00-*` must stay FIRST: its first line is the fonts `@import`, which is only
  valid at the top of its sheet.

## Cache discipline (web + PWA)

- After changing CSS/JS, bump `?v=` in `index.html`.
- Every new local asset MUST be added to `PRECACHE` in `sw.js` AND `CACHE_NAME`
  bumped (`rtlmd-vN`) — otherwise installed PWAs never receive it.
- Test with a fresh `?cb=xxx` buster: a stale cached 301 (`/ → /fa` from an old
  server config) can masquerade as a server bug. `?cb=` bypasses it.

## Build & release

- New build steps go into the `vendor` chain in `package.json`
  (`pack`/`dist` depend on it). Always `npm run vendor` before packaging.
- `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.build/` are gitignored; generated bundles ship.

## Verification (do this before calling anything done)

1. `npm run build:js` passes (syntax gate + dup guard).
2. Browser smoke on `http://rtlmd.test/?cb=xxx`: full render, all
   `window.rtlmd*` hooks = `function`, TOC builds, find panel, settings dialog,
   REAL `window.rtlmdExportDocx()` path (button disables → re-enables, no alert).
3. `?selfcheck=1` → no failure alert (exercises titles, escape, DOMPurify
   sanitize, Word-HTML builder, scroll-sync ranges).
4. New/changed assets all return HTTP 200.
5. If structure changed, update the file list note at the end of `PRD.md`.

## Refactor discipline

Mechanical moves only: every source line must land in exactly one new home
(conservation), no behavior change, no new features smuggled in. Confirm with
the user before changing runtime behavior or the file layout.
